    pr_ref:  # 577d
    description: "Discovered while reframing INV-pitab symptom 2. The per-pass toolchain field and run_signature are NOT cache keys (run_signature has zero consumers; its 'for cache keying' docstring is false). The real cache is ~/.cache/hypergumbo/<repo_fingerprint>/results/<state_hash>/<analyzer_identity>/ (sketch_embeddings._get_results_cache_dir). None of the three segments captures grammar version. reproducibility_context already DETECTS grammar versions for the top-level block but the cache never consults them."  # 577d
    fields:  # 577d
      statement: "The hypergumbo results cache must invalidate when any input that affects analysis output changes. The tree-sitter grammar version affects output but is absent from all three cache-key segments (repo_fingerprint, state_hash, analyzer_identity), so a grammar upgrade serves stale cached results."  # 577d
      root_cause: "compute_analyzer_identity_hash (analyzer_identity.py) hashes hypergumbo_core.__version__ + the .py content of every installed hypergumbo_* package. tree-sitter grammar packages (tree_sitter_rust, tree-sitter-language-pack, ...) are NOT hypergumbo_* packages, so their versions never enter the identity hash. repo_fingerprint/state_hash key only on target-repo content (path:size:mtime). Net: upgrading a grammar between two runs on the same unchanged repo with the same hypergumbo version yields a cache HIT on results produced by the OLD grammar. Confirmed behaviorally: _get_results_cache_dir returns a byte-identical path (analyzer_identity 5ca857265b4683d3) after a simulated grammar upgrade. Fix: fold _detect_tree_sitter_versions() output (ts lib + grammar pkg versions) into compute_analyzer_identity_hash. Tradeoff: global identity over-invalidates (any grammar upgrade rebuilds whole cache); per-language granularity deferred as future optimization."  # 577d
